Lok Vault – Privacy Policy
An Ads free experience,
Effective Date: Immediately upon installation

This Privacy Policy describes how Lok Vault ("the App") collects, uses, stores, and protects your information. By using the App, you agree to the practices described in this policy.

1. Introduction

Lok Vault is an offline vault application designed to securely store your personal photos, videos, and private files on your device. The App does not require an internet connection to function and does not upload, share, or transmit any personal data to external servers.

2. Information We Collect
2.1 User-Provided Information

Vault Password/Grid Selection: The unique grid-based password you create is stored locally on your device, using simple preferences storage.

Imported Photos & Videos: Any media you import into the vault is stored only on your device inside an app-specific private folder.

App Settings: Theme preference, hidden item settings, biometric unlock option, and album organization are stored locally.

2.2 Automatically Collected Information

Lok Vault does not collect or transmit analytics, personal identifiers, device data, or any form of tracking information.

3. How We Use Your Information

Since all data remains on your device, we use your stored information only to:

Authenticate you using your selected grid password never stored by us.

Enable local biometric unlock (if enabled).

Display and manage your stored media files.

Maintain settings and preferences for your convenience.

No information is sent to external servers.

4. Data Storage & Security

All files, settings, and vault data are stored locally on your device.

The App does not store your data outside your device.

Because the app is fully offline, no external parties have access to your vault.

Although we use simple local storage as per your preference, your device's security features (screen lock, OS-level encryption, biometrics) add protection.

5. Biometric Authentication

If enabled, the App uses your device's built‑in biometric authentication (fingerprint or face unlock) through your device’s secure system APIs.

No biometric data is collected or stored by Lok Vault.

The App only receives confirmation of successful authentication from the device.

6. Permissions We Request

To function properly, Lok Vault may request the following permissions:

Storage / Photos & Media Access: To import, store, and manage your media files locally.

Biometric / Device Credential: To enable biometric unlock.

These permissions are used strictly offline and solely for features you enable.

7. Third‑Party Services

Lok Vault does not use third‑party analytics, advertising networks, cloud services, or data processors. It is a fully offline App.

8. Children's Privacy

Lok Vault does not target or intentionally collect information from children under 13. Since no data is transmitted externally, the App does not gather identifiable information from any user.

9. Your Rights

Since all data stays on your device, you retain complete control. You can:

Delete your vault items at any time.

Uninstall the App to remove all data permanently.

No remote data exists to request access to, modify, or delete.

10. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. Any updates will be included in the App or in future versions.

